WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.120
Thanks to the box office success of Jigsaw,
it looks like we'll be getting a ninth Saw

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:10.099
movie in the next couple years.

00:00:10.099 --> 00:00:14.160
I think the filmmakers counted on this happening,
because they seem to have left little clues

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.869
like this one, to set up the next installment.

00:00:16.869 --> 00:00:19.760
Before we get this started, I know what you
people are going to say.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:21.600
"Oh, Hoffman could still be alive.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.300
Bobby Dagan could be a disciple of Jigsaw!

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.599
Blah blah blah!"

00:00:25.599 --> 00:00:26.930
And to that, I say...

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.029
Hoffman is dead, OK?

00:00:28.029 --> 00:00:31.039
He's chained in the same spot that Adam was
in the original Saw.

00:00:31.039 --> 00:00:35.750
We all know there's only one way out of that
Gordon clearly throws away the key.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.610
As for the others, I'll do a full rundown
of who I think might be alive and possibly

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:41.430
appearing in Saw IX.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:46.040
But honestly, I don't see anyone from the
original 7 movies making a return.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.190
I mean, what was the point of Jigsaw if not
to freshen things up and bring the franchise

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.309
back to theaters?

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:55.510
We got all new characters, and I don't think
any of the other sequels had a total of zero

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:57.320
flashbacks to other movies.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.350
Even the title, breaking the numeric sequence
of Saw films just tells me that this is supposed

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.840
to be a fresh slate in a way.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:07.390
It wasn't my favorite Saw film by any means,
but I do admire the way it revived the property

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:11.929
without relying on a reboot to wipe away the
glorious continuity that's been established.

00:01:11.929 --> 00:01:15.810
And I think it did a great job of laying the
foundations for Saw IX, so that's exactly

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:16.829
where I'll start.

00:01:16.829 --> 00:01:20.219
The big question going into the new movie
is who's going to be the next Jigsaw?

00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:24.240
In the last movie, we saw Logan Nelson replicating
Jigsaw's teachings.

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.880
At first it would appear that Nelson is a
corrupt Jigsaw because he, like Hoffman, uses

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.390
the Jigsaw image for personal vendetta and
selfish reasons.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:36.909
However, in the final moments, Nelson reveals
that everyone he puts into his game deserved

00:01:36.909 --> 00:01:39.289
to be there under John Kramer's ideals.

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:42.880
He mentions that the first three people in
his game were criminals that got off the hook

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.130
that were similar to the players in Jigsaw's
original game.

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:50.689
Remember, the game we saw in the movie was
John Kramer's game from 10 years ago.

00:01:50.689 --> 00:01:55.069
We only actually see little glimpses of Nelson's
game and the victims.

00:01:55.069 --> 00:01:57.630
The last two players were Halloran and Nelson.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:02:01.130
Halloran deserves to be there because he's
the one who took bribes and got those criminals

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:04.700
off the hook, including the murderer of Nelson's
wife.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.590
And then there's Nelson himself, who switched
the labels on John Kramer's brain scan and

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:10.050
never got punished for it.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:14.300
He never woke up from John Kramer's sedative
in time to play the game in which he was originally

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.690
supposed to be tested.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:20.360
So he put himself in his own game in order
to test himself and see if he was as talented

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.410
as Jigsaw.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:25.250
This also replicates John putting himself
in the room in the original Saw.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:29.280
Everything seems to add up towards him being
the perfect successor to Jigsaw.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:33.201
Some might argue that Nelson can't really
continue being Jigsaw in a future movie, but

00:02:33.201 --> 00:02:35.260
I think there's evidence that he can.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:39.690
Unlike John Kramer, who tends to leave the
corpses in his secret locations, Nelson moves

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.780
his to be discovered by the public.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.500
But he doesn't have to do that for Detective
Halloran.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:49.260
Logan has set things up in a way to make everyone
think that Halloran is the new Jigsaw.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:53.810
In fact, the only part he seems to care about
from the audio admission is this:

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:59.750
"Innocent people died because of me I did
it!"

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:05.850
So if Halloran were to disappear now, everyone
would think that he is responsible, allowing

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:09.800
Logan to continue the work of Jigsaw with
new games in the future.

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:11.990
But he makes one mistake.

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:15.500
John Kramer tells him to never allow personal
anger and revenge to interfere.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.670
But as far as I can tell, there's one participant
who never gets a fair chance at redemption,

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:24.040
and that is Edgar Munsen, the man who murdered
Nelson's wife.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:29.090
He seems to be involved in another game setup
by Nelson, and despite appearing to succeed,

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:33.280
Nelson shoots him, takes him off life support
and dumps him in John Kramer's grave.

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:37.730
The original Jigsaw never actually murdered
anyone, but Nelson makes this mistake to avenge

00:03:37.730 --> 00:03:38.730
his wife.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:43.180
He may have faltered off of the path John
Kramer set for him due to the PTSD he picked

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:46.940
up in the army, which you can read about by
pausing here in the movie.

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:51.420
We've already seen what happens when one of
Jigsaw's successors break the rules, the disciples

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:54.250
of Jigsaw come after him to make things right.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:58.790
Even if it's not mentioned in Saw IX, you
can bet that a showdown between Logan Nelson

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:01.640
and the disciples of Jigsaw is coming in the
future.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:03.800
So who's going to be part of this battle?

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:07.710
We know Dr. Lawrence Gordon has played this
part in the past, and he's someone who's definitely

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:09.200
still alive and active.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:13.970
I've speculated on who these other pigmasks
who help Dr. Gordon could be.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:17.380
Some of you in the comments of a previous
video said that they could be minor characters

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:21.459
from the Saw VII opening based on some producers'
commentary track.

00:04:21.459 --> 00:04:26.180
I'm going to go ahead and say that's not canon,
and if that was the intention at one time

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:28.870
it's going to be changed now that they are
continuing the series.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:33.229
I speculated that Nelson may actually be one
of Gordon's assistants, but there are a couple

00:04:33.229 --> 00:04:35.340
of other possibilities as well.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.680
This is where the characters from previous
films could come in.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:42.039
It would make sense that Gordon would work
with any of the other members of the Jigsaw

00:04:42.039 --> 00:04:43.969
survivor group from Saw VII.

00:04:43.969 --> 00:04:46.889
But there are other survivors that weren't
seen in that group.

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:51.199
These include Brent and Tara Abbott from Saw
VI.

00:04:51.199 --> 00:04:56.199
The father of of that family was the guy who
was denied insurance coverage needed to survive,

00:04:56.199 --> 00:04:59.120
so it makes sense that his family would want
to see justice served.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:03.970
I could see Brent, now a fully grown adult,
being a powerful force in a new movie.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:07.759
Another character who would be grown up now
is Daniel Matthews, the son of the Detective

00:05:07.759 --> 00:05:09.050
from Saw II.

00:05:09.050 --> 00:05:10.050
He was also a survivor.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:14.919
It would be easy to see him learning under
John Kramer's wing after losing his father.

00:05:14.919 --> 00:05:19.419
Then we've got Corbett Denlon, a survivor
who lost both of her parents in Saw III.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:22.860
Because Kramer was already gone, she would
have had to have been trained by the corrupt

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:27.150
Mark Hoffman, meaning that if she does end
up appearing again, she might actually be

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.009
more on Nelson's side.

00:05:29.009 --> 00:05:33.319
Then there's Pamela Jenkins, the reporter
who sensationalized Jigsaw stories for her

00:05:33.319 --> 00:05:34.790
own personal gain.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:38.260
She'd be another candidate to be on Nelson's
side, because she may have been corrupted

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:39.479
by Hoffman.

00:05:39.479 --> 00:05:42.979
By the way, Nelson does have anonymous people
helping him too.

00:05:42.979 --> 00:05:47.910
It could be cool in a future movie to see
two Jigsaws and their followers engaged in

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:49.659
a war of ideals.

00:05:49.659 --> 00:05:53.980
But like I said before, I think it's unlikely
we'll see the return of old characters, because

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:58.630
the new Jigsaw film sets up the possibility
for new Pig Mask minions as well.

00:05:58.630 --> 00:06:02.509
Eleanor is an obvious candidate, due to her
fandom for Jigsaw and the fact that Nelson

00:06:02.509 --> 00:06:03.990
is grooming her throughout the movie.

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:08.710
The last we see of her in Jigsaw shows her
getting picked up after escaping the pig farm,

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:13.199
and she's got a look of fear on her face,
so maybe someone from the survivor group has

00:06:13.199 --> 00:06:14.199
plans for her.

00:06:14.199 --> 00:06:18.550
There's also the fansite she spends all that
time on, Jigsaw Rules, which could offer a

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:21.189
new pool of candidates to be assistants.

00:06:21.189 --> 00:06:24.660
Nelson will need the extra help, because there
are plenty more criminals set free during

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:28.449
Halloran regime, and there could be other
corrupt officials as well.

00:06:28.449 --> 00:06:32.009
If you're still not convinced there is going
to be another one, let me direct your attention

00:06:32.009 --> 00:06:34.729
to the news clippings in Eleanor's studio.

00:06:34.729 --> 00:06:41.919
This article from the Saw V era says the story
will be continued on 6, 7, 8 and 9!

00:06:41.919 --> 00:06:46.809
If that's not proof enough for you, then look
at this story which is supposedly about Jigsaw,

00:06:46.809 --> 00:06:50.520
but the contents of the article seem to only
talk about...

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:51.660
Ticketmaster?

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:55.949
They want us to buy tickets to Jigsaw, so
that they can make Saw IX!

00:06:55.949 --> 00:07:00.550
So if you bought tickets to Jigsaw, or if
you're excited about the revival of the franchise,

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.919
let me know by leaving a like on this video.

00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:06.729
Leave your ideas for the next Saw in the comments,
and if there are enough cool ones, maybe I'll

00:07:06.729 --> 00:07:08.610
feature them in a future video.

00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:13.909
And if you haven't already, remember to subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

00:07:13.909 --> 00:07:18.449
that deathbell for notifications and I'll
see you in the next one.

00:07:18.449 --> 00:07:20.279
Assuming we both survive.

